WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.820
My daddy rode a tree out, one of these big oak trees.

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.520
I'll show you when we go outside.

3
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:09.920
He rode in that tree with him, his two sisters and his mom and dad for Hurricane Audrey.

4
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:17.960
But we're standing underneath this other big oak tree and he says, "You know, Bub, that storm comes through, that water's going to be that high."

5
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.200
I'm going to show y'all where that's at.

6
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.280
And I said, "Dad, look, don't tell me this."

7
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.400
He said, "I'm telling you."

8
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:33.280
Well, about two weeks later when we finally all got down here together and standing and my house is completely gone and,

9
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.960
"I want to show you something."

10
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.060
And he's really a smart aleck sometimes, you know, with me.

11
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:47.920
And you can see where the debris right where he pointed at was packed into that branch like that.

12
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.300
He said, "You know the water was that high."

13
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.540
"Yeah, Daddy, I know, the water was that high."

14
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.760
To be so peaceful and tranquil right now, it can be a dirty place.

15
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:04.720
It can be a mean place, and in a flash, as fast as it get here, it's gone again, you know.

16
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.540
I did it twice in my life, threw all my keys away.

17
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:14.080
And then you got a tranquil place that you . . . And look at the monsters outside.

18
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.300
That's giants.

19
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.800
Nothing killed them.

20
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.740
Man killed them.

21
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.160
That's the only thing that will kill that oak tree.

22
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.800
A man can kill it.

23
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.447
Salt water don't kill them unless it stays on it.

24
00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:28.220
But the pecan trees we have, the native pecans, they all dead.

25
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:34.940
The hackberry trees, you used to have them . . . Rita killed them, Ike washed them away.

26
00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.780
But all the old men are still standing out there.
